<sup>† One-sided p-values derived from KDE-smoothed empirical distributions of PFES for the pathogenic (case) and control (benign and common population) variants, computed as the tail area of the KDE beyond the observed score. *p*<sub>enriched</sub>: right-tail area under the control KDE at the variant's PFES, quantifying how enriched the variant's protein feature profile is relative to control variation. *p*<sub>depleted</sub>: left-tail area under the case KDE at the variant's PFES, quantifying how depleted the variant's protein feature profile is relative to pathogenic variation.
    For individual protein feature attributes, p-values are calculated in the same way but using empirical distributions of each attribute-level sub-score. **Bold** values indicate statistical significance (*p* < 0.05).</sup>

<sup>†† *PF-Enriched*: *p*<sub>enriched</sub> < 0.05, variant's PFES falls in the upper tail of the control distribution, indicating overrepresentation of pathogenic-associated protein features.
    *PF-Depleted*: *p*<sub>depleted</sub> < 0.05, variant's PFES falls in the lower tail of the case distribution, indicating overrepresentation of tolerance-associated protein features.
    *PF-Neutral*: statistically consistent with both distributions.</sup>

